            "Accuracy is defined as the average angular offset between the locations of fixations and their targets and is often called validity in social science, while spatial precision is the root-mean-square angular distance between successive samples and corresponds to reliability.",
            "System latency is the average end-to-end delay from an actual eye movement until the recording computer signals that a movement has occurred, and temporal precision is the standard deviation of that latency.",
